        <Section heading="Research gaps" id="gaps">
          <Rows rows={[
            { title: "Daily pass limits (Nov 13)", detail: "Daily pass 2026-11-13: additions are registry/catalogue-verified (217 abstract-level, 440 DOI metadata only, 4 catalogue records, 9 landing pages read) — not full-text reviewed. Many Elsevier items have no abstract in Crossref/OpenAlex, so descriptions are bibliographic only. ~45 no-DOI classics surfaced by the citation chase (TRID/HRB reports, CiNii-listed books such as Bažant's creep monographs and Mehta's Materials Science of Concrete, Czech/Belgian theses incl. the 1950s Purdocement alkali-activated slag study) could not be inspected today (TRID 503, CiNii/JS-only pages) and were not added. ACI symposium papers carry ACI DOIs that are not registered at doi.org. 3 leads open (Kraków Technical Transactions DOIs without Crossref metadata; one Zenodo DOI unregistered)." },
            { title: "Daily pass limits (Nov 12)", detail: "Daily pass 2026-11-12: additions are registry/catalogue-verified (95 abstract-level, 170 DOI metadata only, 2 catalogue records, 1 landing pages read) — not full-text reviewed. Many Elsevier journal items have no abstract in Crossref/OpenAlex, so descriptions are bibliographic only. Non-English coverage is still thin (German/French/Spanish/Portuguese journal and standards literature, JIS/GB/IS national standards); Chinese journals registered only with ChinaDOI/CNKI are hard to verify (1 lead open). Historical ACI committee reports in ACI journals carry no committee designation in Crossref. Legacy Type IL topics (standards, dot, carbon, fresh) still need PLC-specific DOT specifications and EPD sources." },
            { title: "Daily pass limits (Nov 11)", detail: "Daily pass 2026-11-11: candidate queue is empty (0 open). New additions are registry/catalogue-verified (48 abstract-level, 81 DOI metadata only, 14 catalogue records, 4 landing pages read) — not full-text reviewed. Citation chasing was not done this pass; thin topics remain cross-supply-region (regional cement/aggregate market data beyond emissions papers), RCC dam construction practice reports (USACE/USBR), and non-English national cement standards (JIS, GB, IS) — Japanese/Chinese standards bodies not reachable via Crossref." },
            { title: "Lead verification limits (Nov 10)", detail: "1,109 queue leads were promoted on registry metadata (693 with abstracts): verified to exist and to be on-topic, not full-text reviewed. 4 leads stay open: Theory and Experiments on the Mechanical Behaviour of Cracks; Densified Cement/Ultrafine Particle-based Materials; THE NIBBLER--A NEW CONCEPT IN CONCRETE BREAKING; AGGREGATES FROM WASTE MATERIALS." },
            { title: "Deep pass 3 limits (Nov 10)", detail: "Pass 3 is another batch, not complete coverage. 57 of 114 new records are DOI-metadata-only and 46 abstract-level; only 8 full text. Normative texts of ACI 318-25, EN 206-1:2026, ACI PRC-522-23 and ASTM C1897 not read (previews/news only). Illinois and Texas repositories, USACE library and TU Delft were unreachable from this network; their items stay in the candidate queue (1,255 open)." },
            { title: "Deep pass 2 limits (Nov 9)", detail: "Pass 2 (2026-11-09) is a second batch, not complete coverage. Many pass-2 records are DOI/abstract-level (closed full text); access level is recorded per record in research/portable/verified-sources.jsonl. Still open: China GB 175 / India IS standards, ACI 544/237R/303R/207 texts, USACE/USBR RCC dam manuals, ASTM C91/C270/C618 current-edition reviews, refractory castables practice." },
            { title: "Field performance data", detail: "Lab-to-field correlation and performance-based specs still developing." },
            { title: "Partly covered now", detail: "Shotcrete (one 2026 ACI study), 3D printing (three lab studies including Nature Comm R132), SCC (2018 Georgia Tech dissertation). Mass concrete topic expanded (R105-R124) plus PINN hydration-heat surrogate (R128)." },
            { title: "Not yet covered by found sources", detail: "Ready-mix Type IL market cost series (R132 TEA has retail PLC/limestone unit costs only); primary ACI 318/301 code text (ACA hub R138 is secondary); EN 197-1 official text." },
            { title: "Microcracking in Type IL", detail: "R127 addresses Type IL paste microstructure/carbonation with nanosilica, but no direct study yet images ITZ microcracks in commercial Type IL vs OPC concrete, separates limestone aggregate from filler effects, or applies DIC to PLC." },
            { title: "Mass concrete with Type IL", detail: "No field case study of a Type IL mass pour with temperature monitoring; PINN (R128) is modeling only; no same-clinker adiabatic IL vs I/II comparison other than FDOT; DEF with PLC only in lab studies; no DOT other than Florida addresses Type IL in its mass spec; ACI 207 is silent on Type IL." },
          ]} />
          <LinkCards links={links("gaps")} />
        </Section>

